{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with Hb Mizuho may be splenectomized at a young age to decrease their need for blood transfusions. OBSERVATIONS: Transfusion-dependency decreased dramatically in a 4-year-old white boy with Hb Mizuho after splenectomy. Surprisingly, he developed reticulocytosis (>1000×10 9 /L) with a peak reticulocyte percentage of 49%, and erythrocyte abnormalities, including Heinz bodies, Howell-Jolly bodies, and basophilic stippling. Manual reticulocyte counting and flow cytometric measurement with anti-CD71 antibodies supported a truly elevated reticulocyte count. CONCLUSIONS: We propose possible explanations for the extreme reticulocytosis that arose postsplenectomy and compare the reticulocyte count in the present case with previously published cases.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bøttger, Helene Narvestad","Winther-Larsen, Anne","Thomsen, Jens Haugbølle","Dziegiel, Morten Hanefeld","Hansen, Anne Todsen","Hasle, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.56-751785"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Child Preschool","Hb Mizuho","Hemoglobinopathy","Humans","Male","Reticulocytosis","Splenectomy","Splenectomy adverse effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extreme reticulocytosis after splenectomy in a patient with hemoglobin mizuho","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181586201","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.56-751785","identifier":[{"id":"85181586201","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38011049","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c99ef507-da92-4683-b5d4-1c904acce126","ku-b31bb4b2-b6d2-432b-96c4-1546cc5dc381"],"keyword":["Child, Preschool","Erythrocyte Inclusions","Hb Mizuho","Hemoglobins, Abnormal","Humans","Male","Reticulocytosis","Splenectomy/adverse effects","hemoglobinopathy","splenectomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-789D566241162DDA71F17D165F6FAC95"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department for Clinical Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical immunology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene","key":"narvestadbøttgerpau","last":"Narvestad-Bøttger","locid":"3a20c113-14f9-4df5-b0f9-cbd318f6876a","name":"Bøttger, Helene Narvestad","name_org":"Narvestad-Bøttger, Helene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"wintherlarsenpau","last":"W